course: dictionary
lesson: 3436
title: Learning a word from its examples
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An eyelid is the thin fold of skin that closes over your eye when you blink or sleep. You can feel your eyelids move every time you blink.
explain: The examples show how the word is used. «Snakes have no eyelids; a clear scale covers each eye.» The clue is the word no: a snake has no fold of skin over its eye, so something else, a clear scale, does the job.
explain: «A crocodile's eyes, ears and nostrils are on top of its head, and a clear third eyelid protects its eyes under water like goggles.» Here third eyelid is a different fold, so you can see that a crocodile has more than the usual two.
explain: Some words appear in set phrases. «Without batting an eyelid» means showing no surprise at all. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: An eyelid is the thin fold of skin that closes over your eye.
fact: «Eyelids» is the plural, meaning more than one eyelid.
fact: Eyelids protect your eyes from dust and light, and blinking spreads tears to keep your eyes wet.
fact: «Heavy eyelids» shows a sleepy character in a story.
fact: «Upper eyelid» and «lower eyelid» name the top and bottom folds of skin.
exercise: Which word means the thin fold of skin that closes over your eye? | Eyelash | Eyebrow | *Eyelid | Eyeball
exercise: «Snakes have no eyelids; a clear scale covers each eye.» What does this tell you about snakes? | They blink faster than people | They can close their eyes for a long sleep | They have three eyelids | *Their eyes are covered by a clear scale instead of an eyelid
exercise: «Without batting an eyelid» means what? | Blinking very fast | Crying for a long time | *Showing no surprise at all | Closing your eyes to sleep
test: «The potoo sits still on a branch looking exactly like a dead stump, and even with its eyes shut it can see through notches in its eyelids.» Which word in this sentence is the plural of eyelid? | *eyelids | notches | branch | stump
test: A story says a girl had «heavy eyelids». What does this show? | She could see in the dark | She was very angry | She was about to sing | *She was sleepy
exam: According to the examples, which is true about a crocodile's eyes? | Its eyes are on the bottom of its head | Its eyelids are made of glass | *It has a clear third eyelid that protects its eyes under water | It has no eyelids at all
